+# Garage entry restored ? 2026-11-06
+
+The owner rejects the new full-screen loading window before opening Garage. Garage now follows its earlier direct page transition. The existing in-page car preview preparation and retained live showroom remain; this change removes the separate logo/progress/Cancel screen introduced by the performance task.
+
+**GER01:** One runtime line changes in `game/core/app.gd`: first-use feature-cover admission now applies to Editor/Drafts only. Garage's existing controller builds the page through the original path. Warm entry still reuses the same Garage page. Profile paging, checkpoint artifacts, staged automatic header preparation, car quality and race loading are retained.
+
+**GERQ01:** The navigation regression now observes actual scene-tree additions and requires zero `FeatureLoadingScreen` nodes during both cold and warm Garage entry. It also verifies immediate Garage page installation, controller installation and retained page identity. Editor account cancellation and race-cover/navigation checks remain. The obsolete Garage-modal Cancel assertions are replaced by the owner's new no-modal requirement.
+
+Focused native tests pass **22/0 on Compatibility and 22/0 on desktop Mobile**, with cold/warm Garage captures. The isolated real-App flow passes **24/0**, including a fully prepared live car, both reflections, Editor/race entry, canonical tick 0/full countdown/five laps, retained reopening and account-owner replacement. All three accepted runs have unchanged sources during execution and no script errors. Direct desktop runs retain the environment's root-certificate-store diagnostic.
+
+An initial full-App run passed 24/0 while an unrelated `electric_glass.gdshader` changed concurrently. That run is retained with its source-change receipt and is not the final isolated qualification. The tablet package is built from the last deployed **9d328fb6e64cdf51f72c95abc68c1d5f** source snapshot with only this one-line runtime fix. Before applying the fix, recalculating the entire shipping source identity reproduced 9d exactly. After export it still reproduces the new **29b1076458152408e5486a7b4eec2d4b** identity. Concurrent shader work remains in the shared workspace and is excluded from this tablet update; the main workspace's generated version was not overwritten with the isolated build's identity.
+
+**GERD01:** The new ARM64 APK is installed over the previous tablet app. Export uses the standard pinned `scripts/dev.ps1 -Action ExportAndroid -AndroidPreset "Android ARM64" -QuickValidation -CommandTimeoutSeconds 600` in the isolated root, with private offline PC test data and the existing signing setup. Export succeeds in 742.782 seconds. Prepared assets 468/1925checks/0failures, five exact photographs/156 source hashes, import/startup, driving 72/0, catalogue 21/0 and menus 41/0 pass. All 8,917 APK ZIP checksums and actual ARM64 libraries validate. No runtime/visual source changed during the successful export.
+
+Installed APK: **323,432,566 bytes**, SHA-256 **ffe768c376b588734bab6404639c236f26f55775e1a14cee7434581a1117ff95**, package `org.circuit01.handlinglab`, version **0.3.0-creator.29b1076458152408e5486a7b4eec2d4b**. The installed file hash matches the exported artifact. All **772 existing app files** match exactly immediately before/after replacement and before launch, and the original first-install timestamp is unchanged. No uninstall, data clearing or track sync occurs. The prior 9d APK remains in `build/garage-entry-restore-20261106/previous-installed.apk` for rollback.
+
+After the owner manually unlocked the secure keyguard, the installed process resumed and reached `APP_READY` with actual game-window focus. First Garage entry and a normal Race-to-Garage revisit were inspected on the tablet: the original showroom and saved car appear without the new full-screen loading window. No matched script/parser/fatal/invalid-access errors were recorded. [Tablet Garage](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/tablet-garage.png) and [revisit](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/tablet-garage-warm.png) retain the views; the app is left in Garage. The initial secure-keyguard timeout remains recorded; no credential was read or entered. This is a UI/startup smoke check, not a performance benchmark or full gameplay acceptance.
+
+The isolated build first required process-scoped Git trust for its task-owned repository and a local copy of the existing pinned Android source ZIP. Both failed setup attempts remain recorded; no global Git policy was changed and no toolchain download was needed. Its first import was slow but completed before the attempted stop; that stop found no process and terminated nothing. The build continued through every required check. Existing catalogue-anchor and embedded-text-data export warnings remain.
+
+[Validation](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/validation.json), [isolation proof](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/isolation.json), [export](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/export-result.json) and [deployment](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/deployment.json) retain commands, source hashes, results and boundaries. Native captures are under `focused-compatibility`, `focused-mobile` and `isolated-retained-flow/result-views`. Raw build/device logs and private file manifests remain in `build/garage-entry-restore-20261106`; private account manifests are not copied into documentation.
+
+The actual production code delta is the Garage routing line; `game/tests/test_feature_navigation.gd` contains the updated behavioral regression. Generated build metadata lives in the isolated export. No direct backend/admin action, purchase/authentication flow, PC save change or renderer/physics/quality change is part of this correction. The main Git index is untouched. Cold resource work still runs synchronously and can delay a frame as before; removing the window is a presentation restoration, not a loading-speed claim.
+
+[Task-only patch](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/task.patch), [file manifest](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/manifest.json) and [strict forward/reverse checkpoint](evidence/garage-entry-restore-2026-11-06/checkpoint.json).
